-- examples/checks/retract-last-read.rofl — THE LAST FACT OF A RELATION TAKEN BACK WHERE A RULE READS edb. rl_lone
-- names the relations no load declares; retracting rr_gone(1), the only fact of its relation, takes edb(rr_gone)
-- with it, and the rule reading edb concludes what a load without the fact concludes. The Rust engine evaluates
-- again and says why. Both engines.
rr_name(rr_gone). rr_name(rr_kept).
rr_gone(1).
rr_kept(1).
rl_lone(R) :- rr_name(R), not edb(R).
-- expect-row: rl_lone[main](rr_gone)
-- expect-no-row: rl_lone[main](rr_kept)
